{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-718", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/718", "wordCount": 2829, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello. My name is Simon"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Gladman and I'm with the Vector"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "and Numerics group."}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "In this presentation, I'll be"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "talking about two topics."}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "First, our new Swift Overlay for"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "Accelerate."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "And second, measuring"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "Accelerate's performance using"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "the Linpack benchmark."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "Before we dive into the Swift"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "Overlay, let's recap exactly"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "what the Accelerate framework"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "is. The primary purpose of"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "Accelerate is to provide"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "thousands of low-level math"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "primitives that run on a CPU and"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "support image and signal"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "processing, vector arithmetic,"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "linear algebra, and machine"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "learning."}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "Most of these primitives are"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "hand tuned to the"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "microarchitecture of the"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "processor."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "This means we get excellent"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "performance and this performance"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "translates directly into energy"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "savings."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "So, if you're an app developer"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "and you use the Accelerate"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "framework, not only will your"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "application run faster, but"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "you'll also use less battery"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "life."}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "We provide the primitives across"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "all of Apple's platforms."}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "This includes not only macOS and"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "iOS but watchOS and tvOS as"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "well."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "This means your users are going"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "to have an overall better"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "Accelerate's libraries are"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "immensely powerful but up until"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "now, their interfaces weren't"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "that friendly to Swift"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "developers."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "We've looked at four libraries"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "and created new Swift-friendly"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "APIs to make using Acclerate in"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "Swift projects really easy."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "The four libraries we focused on"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "are vDSP that provides digital"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "signal processing routines"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "including arithmetic on large"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "vectors, Fourier transforms,"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "biquadratic filtering, and"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "powerful type conversion."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "vForce that provides arithmetic"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "and transcendental functions"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "including trig and logarithmic"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "routines."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "Quadrature, that's dedicated to"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "the numerical integration of"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "functions."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "And vImage, that provides a huge"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "selection of image processing"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "functions and integrates easily"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "with core graphics and core"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "video."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "Accelerate gets its performance"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "benefits by using vectorization."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "To understand vectorization,"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "let's first look at a simple"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "calculation over the elements of"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "an array using scalar code."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "If, for example, you're writing"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "code that multiplies each"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "element of one array with the"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "corresponding element in"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "another, and you're using a four"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "loop, each pair of elements are"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "separately loaded, multiplied"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "together, and the results"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "stored."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "So, after the first elements in"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "A and B are multiplied together"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "to calculate the first element"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "in C, the second pair are"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "processed."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "Then, the third."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "And, finally, the fourth."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "However, if you're processing"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "the elements of an array using"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "Accelerate, your calculation is"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "performed on single instruction"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "multiple data, or simD"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "registers."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "These registers can perform the"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "same instruction on multiple"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "items of data by packing those"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "multiple items into a single"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "register."}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "For example, a single 128-bit"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "register can actually store four"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "32-bit floating point values."}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "So, a vectorized multiply"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "operation can simultaneously"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "multiply four pairs of elements"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "at a time."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "This means that not only will"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "the task be quicker, it will"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "also be significantly more"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "energy efficient."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "The multiply function we just"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "looked at part of Accelerate's"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "digital signal processing"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "library, vDSP."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "So, let's begin by looking at"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "how the new Swift API simplifies"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "using vDSP."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "vDSP provides vectorized digital"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "signal processing functions"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "including Fourier transforms,"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "biquadratic filtering,"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "convolution, and correlation."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "Furthermore, vDSP also provides"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "some powerful, more general"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "functions including element-wise"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "arithmetic and type conversion."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "So, even if you don't have an"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "immediate need to, for example,"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "compute the coherence of two"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "signals, you may find that"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "vDSP's general computation"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "routines offer a solution to"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "improve your app's performance."}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "Let's take a look at some basic"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "arithmetic."}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "An example could be given four"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "arrays of single-precision"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "values, you need to calculate"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "the element-wise sum of two of"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "the array's the element-wise"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "difference in the other two, and"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "multiply those results with each"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "other."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "Using a four loop is a perfectly"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "reasonable solution to this"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "problem and calculates the"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "expected results."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "Here's how you perform that"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "calculation using vDSP's classic"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "API."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "Using vDSP is approximately"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "three times faster than the four"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "loop."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "Here's the same computation"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "using our new Swift API for"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "vDSP."}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "We're exposing the new"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "Swift-friendly functions through"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "our vDSP namespace and you can"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "see the function and parameter"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "names explain the operation."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "Because the new functions work"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "with familiar types including"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "arrays and array slices rather"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "than pointers, you no longer"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "need to explicitly pass the"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "count."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "So, the entire function call is"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "clearer and more concise."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "Passing an initialized result"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "array offers the best"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "performance and you can"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "obviously reuse that array in"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "other operations for further"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "performance benefits."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "However, we're also providing"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "self-allocating functions."}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "These make use of Swift's new"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "ability to access an array's"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "uninitialized buffer to return"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "the result of a computation."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "Although not quite as fast as"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "passing existing storage, it's"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "still faster than the scalar"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "approach and, in some cases,"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "will simplify your code."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "Another common task that vDSP"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "can vectorize is type"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "conversion."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "This example converts an array"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "containing double precision"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "values to 16-bit unsigned"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "integer values rounding toward"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "zero."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "The scalar version uses map with"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "explicit rounding."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "Again, this is a perfectly"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "reasonable technique to use, but"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "vDSP can vectorize this task to"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "improve performance."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "In this example, vDSP is"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "approximately four times faster"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "than the previous scalar"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "implementation."}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "The new Swift version of the"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "vDSP function offers a clear"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "interface."}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "The function accepts a source"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "array. The integer type you ought to"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "convert each element to, and an"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "enumeration to specify the"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "rounding."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "vDSP provides Fourier transforms"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "for transforming one-dimensional"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "and two-dimensional data between"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "the time domain and the"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "frequency domain."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "A forward Fourier transform of a"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "signal decomposes it into its"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "component sign waves."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "That's the frequency domain"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "representation."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Conversely, an inverse transform"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "of that frequency domain"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "representation recreates the"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "original signal and that's the"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "time domain representation."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "Fourier transforms have many"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "uses in both signal and image"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "processing."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "For example, once an audio"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "signal has been forward"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "transformed, you can easily"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "reduce or increase certain"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "frequencies to equalize the"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "audio."}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "The classic API is reasonably"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "easy to follow if you're"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "familiar with it."}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "You begin by creating a setup"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "object specifying the number of"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "elements you want to transform"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "and the direction."}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "Then, after creating two arrays"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "to receive results, you call the"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "execute function."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Once you're done, you need to"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "remember to destroy the setup to"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "free the resources allocated to"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "it. The new API simplifies the"}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "instantiation of the setup"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "object and the transform itself"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "is a method with parameter names"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "on the DFT instance."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "And now you don't need to worry"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "about freeing the resources."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "We do that for you."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "And much like the vDSP functions"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "we've looked at, there's a"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "self-allocating version of the"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "transform function that creates"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "and returns the result's arrays"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "for you."}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "If you work with audio data, you"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "may be familiar with biquadratic"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "or biquad filtering."}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "Biquad filters can be used to"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "equalize audio to shape the"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "frequency response, allowing you"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "to, for example, remove either"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "low or high frequencies."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "vDSP's biquad feature operates"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "on single and multichannel"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "signals, and uses a set of"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "individual filter objects called"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "sections."}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "The filters are cascaded; that"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "is, they are set up in a"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "sequence and the entire signal"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "passes through each filter in"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "turn."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "The filters are defined by a"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "series of coefficients that plug"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "into the equation shown here."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "In this example, these values"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "form a low pass filter; that is,"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "a filter that reduces high"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "frequencies."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "Here's the code using vDSP's"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "classic API to create the biquad"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "setup using the coefficients in"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "the previous slide."}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "And here's the code to apply"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "that biquad filter to an array"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "named signal, returning the"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "result to an array named output."}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "Let's look at the same"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "functionality implemented with a"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "new API."}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "As you can see, the new API"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "vastly simplifies the creation"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "of the biquad structure."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "You simply pass the coefficients"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "to the biquad initializer and"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "specify the number of channels"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "and sections."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "Applying the biquad filter to a"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "signal is a single function"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "call."}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "Now, let's look at the new API"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "we've created for Accelerate's"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "library for fast mathematical"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "operations on large arrays,"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "vForce."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "vForce provides transcendental"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "functions not included in vDSP."}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "These include exponential,"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "logarithmic, and trig"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "operations."}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "A typical example of vForce"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "would be to calculate the square"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "root of each element in a large"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "array."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "The scalar version of this code"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "could use map."}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "vForce provides a vectorized"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "function to calculate the square"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "roots that in some situations"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "can be up to 10 times faster"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "than the scalar implementation."}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "The new Swift overlay offers an"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "API that's consistent with the"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "new vDSP functions and provides"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "the performance and energy"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "efficiency benefits of"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "vectorization."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "And much like we've seen"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "earlier, there's a self-allocating version that"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "returns an array containing the"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "square roots of each element in"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "the supplied array."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "Next, we'll take a look at the"}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "new API we've created for"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "Quadrature."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "Quadrature is a historic term"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "for determining the area under a"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "curve."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "It provides an approximation of"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "the definite integrative"}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "function over a finite or"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "infinite interval."}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "In this example, we'll use"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "Quadrature to approximate the"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "area of a semicircle, shown here"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "in green, by integrating the"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "functions shown."}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "Much like the Biquad code for"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "vDSP, there's a fair amount of"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "code required to use the"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "existing Quadrature API."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "The first step is to define a"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "structure that describes a"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "function to integrate."}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "The second step is to define the"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "integration options including"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "the integration algorithm."}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "Finally, with the function on"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "options defined, you can perform"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "the integration using the"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Quadrature integrate function."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "The new API simplifies the code."}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "One great advantage is that you"}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "can specify the integrand, that"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "is, the function to be"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "integrated, as a trading closure"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "rather than as a C function"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "pointer."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "This means you can easily pass"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "values into the integrand."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "Also note that integrators are"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "now enumerations with associated"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "values."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "So, there's no need to supply"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "unnecessary points for interval"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "or maximum intervals here."}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "For example, you can pass the"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "enumeration for the globally"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "adaptive integrator specifying"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "the points for interval and"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "maximum intervals."}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "Now, let's look at the new API"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "we've created for Accelerate's"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "image processing library,"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "vImage."}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "vImage is a library containing a"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "rich collection of image"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "processing tools."}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "It's designed to work seamlessly"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "with both core graphics and core"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "video. It includes operations such as"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "alpha blending, format"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "conversions, histogram"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "operations, convolution,"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "geometry, and morphology."}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "Our new Swift API introduces"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "lots of new features that makes"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "using vImage in Swift easier and"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "more concise."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "We've implemented flags as an"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "option set."}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "vImages throw Swift errors."}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "And we've hidden some of the"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "requirements for mutability and"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "working with unmanaged types."}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "If you're working with core"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "graphics images, there's a"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "common workflow to get that"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "image data into a vImage buffer."}, {"start": 815.0, "text": "First, you need to create a"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "description of the CG images"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "format."}, {"start": 820.0, "text": "Then, instantiate a vImage"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "buffer."}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "Initialize that buffer from the"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "And finally, check for errors in"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "a non-Swift way."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "And that's a lot of boilerplate"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "code for a common operation."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "The new API wraps up all of that"}, {"start": 835.0, "text": "code into a single throwable"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "initializer."}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "However, since we're going to"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "use a CG images format later,"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "here's similar functionality"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "implemented in two steps with a"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "new API."}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "We've added a new initializer to"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "CG image format using a CG"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "image, and an alternative buffer"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "initializer that accepts a CG"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "image and an explicit format"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "description."}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "Once you're finished working"}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "with a buffer, here's the"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "classic vImage function to"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "create a CG image from the"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "buffer's contents."}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "And our new API simplifies that"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "operation too with a new create"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "CG image method that uses the"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "format we've just generated from"}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "the image."}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "One important use case for"}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "vImage is converting between"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "different domains and different"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "formats."}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "vImage's any-to-any convertors"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "can convert between core video"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "and core graphics, and convert"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "between different core graphics"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "formats."}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "For example, you might want to"}, {"start": 895.0, "text": "convert a CMYK core graphics"}, {"start": 897.0, "text": "image to RGB."}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "The existing API to create a"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "convertor accepts the source and"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "destination formats for the"}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "conversion and returns an"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "unmanaged convertor."}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "You take the managed reference"}, {"start": 912.0, "text": "of the convertor and pass that"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "to the function that does the"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "conversion."}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "Our new API adds a new static"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "make function to the existing"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "convertor type that returns a"}, {"start": 922.0, "text": "convertor instance."}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "The conversion is done with the"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "convert method on the convertor"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "instance."}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "Finally, let's look at working"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "with core video image formats."}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "In a typical example, you may"}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "want to create an image format"}, {"start": 939.0, "text": "description from a core video"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "pixel buffer and calculate its"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "channel count."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "Here's the code required by the"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "classic vImage API to create an"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "image format description from a"}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "pixel buffer and get its channel"}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "count."}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "The new API provides the same"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "functionality in two lines of"}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "code."}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "You create an instance of a core"}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "video image format from a pixel"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "buffer using a new static make"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "function."}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "And simply access its channel"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "count as a property."}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "That was a quick tour of a"}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "fraction of the new API."}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "Let's now take a look at Linpack"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "Benchmark and see just how much"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "faster and more energy efficient"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "Accelerate can be."}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "The Linpack Benchmark came out"}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "of the Linpack library which"}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "started as a set of routines for"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "providing fast computational"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "linear algebra."}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "This was later subsumed by a"}, {"start": 994.0, "text": "library called LApack, which"}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "stands for Linear algebra"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "package."}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "LApack was developed to take"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "advantage of these new things at"}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "the time called caches."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "LApack is comprised of many"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "blocked algorithms."}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "These algorit6thms are built on"}, {"start": 1008.0, "text": "top of another library called"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "BLAS, which stands for basic"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "linear algebra subroutines."}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "We'll talk more about BLAS later"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "in this presentation."}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "For now, keep in mind that the"}, {"start": 1018.0, "text": "Linpack Benchmark runs on top of"}, {"start": 1020.0, "text": "LApack, which runs on top of"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "BLAS."}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "The Linpack Benchmark measures"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "how quickly a platform can solve"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "a general system of linear"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "equations."}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "It is comprised of two steps."}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "The matrix factorization step,"}, {"start": 1036.0, "text": "followed by the backsole step."}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "By fixing the algorithm, we're"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "able to see how well different"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "platforms are at running the"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "algorithm."}, {"start": 1044.0, "text": "This provides us with a method"}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "of comparing different"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "platforms."}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "The Linpack Benchmark has"}, {"start": 1049.0, "text": "evolved over time."}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "Originally, it solved a 100 by"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "100 system, and later a 1000 by"}, {"start": 1055.0, "text": "1000 system."}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "The variant most often used"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "today is the no holds barred"}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "variant, where the problem size"}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "can be as large as you want."}, {"start": 1065.0, "text": "This is the variant we will be"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "running today."}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "We are now going to compare"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "Linpack performance on an iPhone"}, {"start": 1072.0, "text": "10S."}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "At the top in orange, we're"}, {"start": 1075.0, "text": "going to run an unoptimized"}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "Linpack."}, {"start": 1078.0, "text": "This Linpack Benchmark does not"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "make use of the accelerate"}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "It relies on software that is"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "not tuned to the process that it"}, {"start": 1085.0, "text": "is running on."}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "Let's see what that looks like."}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "We are now going to compare that"}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "with using the Accelerate"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "framework; that is, we're going"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "to run the same benchmark on the"}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "same platform, but using the"}, {"start": 1099.0, "text": "Accelerate framework which is"}, {"start": 1101.0, "text": "tuned to the platform."}, {"start": 1105.0, "text": "We can see that by using the"}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "Accelerate framework, we are"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "over 24 times faster."}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "This will not only save time,"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "but also energy, which improves"}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "battery life."}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "We're now going to shift gears"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "and take a look at the primary"}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "workhorse routine for the"}, {"start": 1120.0, "text": "Linpack Benchmark called GEMM."}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "As I mentioned earlier, Linpack,"}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "which runs on LApack, is built"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "on top of BLAS."}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "Within BLAS is a routine called"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "GEMM, which stands for general"}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "matrix multiplier."}, {"start": 1136.0, "text": "This routine is used to"}, {"start": 1138.0, "text": "implement several other blocked"}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "routines in BLAS, which are used"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "inside the blocked algorithms at"}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "LApack, most notably the matrix"}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "factorization and solver"}, {"start": 1147.0, "text": "routines."}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "Because of this, GEMM is"}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "sometimes used as a proxy for"}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "performance."}, {"start": 1153.0, "text": "For this presentation, we are"}, {"start": 1155.0, "text": "specifically going to look at"}, {"start": 1156.0, "text": "the single-precision variant of"}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "GEMM."}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "Here, we're going to compare the"}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "performance of the Eigen library"}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "with that of Accelerate."}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "Both the Eigen library and the"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "Accelerate framework will run on"}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "top of an iPhone 10S."}, {"start": 1170.0, "text": "Both will be performing a"}, {"start": 1172.0, "text": "single-precision matrix"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "multiplier."}, {"start": 1174.0, "text": "Let's see how well Eigen does."}, {"start": 1178.0, "text": "Eigen tops out at about 51"}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "gigaflops."}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "Now, let's see how well"}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "Accelerate does."}, {"start": 1184.0, "text": "We can see that the Accelerate"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "framework is almost two and a"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "half times faster than Eigen on"}, {"start": 1190.0, "text": "the same platform."}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "This is because the Accelerate"}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "framework is hand-tuned to the"}, {"start": 1195.0, "text": "platform, allowing us to fully"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "take advantage of what the"}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "platform can offer."}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "So, if you're a developer, using"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "Accelerate in your app will"}, {"start": 1204.0, "text": "offer better performance."}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "This performance translates into"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "less energy, which means better"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "battery life and an overall"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "better experience for your"}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "users."}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "In summary, Accelerate provides"}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "functions for performing"}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "large-scale mathematical"}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "computations and image"}, {"start": 1222.0, "text": "calculations that are fast and"}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "energy efficient."}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "And now we've added a"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "Swift-friendly API that makes"}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "Accelerate's libraries super"}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "easy to work with so your users"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "will benefit from that"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "performance and energy"}, {"start": 1234.0, "text": "efficiency."}, {"start": 1236.0, "text": "Please visit our site where we"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "have samples, articles, and"}, {"start": 1239.0, "text": "extensive reference material"}, {"start": 1241.0, "text": "that covers the entire"}, {"start": 1242.0, "text": "Accelerate framework."}, {"start": 1244.0, "text": "Thank you very much."}]}
